WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.580
Plants often respire roughly half of the energy they fix.

2
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:08.560
So where does the rest go?

3
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.160
Take one square metre for one year, in a made-up budget.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.320
The producers fix 12,000 kilojoules.

5
00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:17.680
That is gross primary production.

6
00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:21.880
The producers respire 6,000 of it, and it leaves as heat.

7
00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:25.660
What is left is net primary production, 6,000.

8
00:00:26.683 --> 00:00:27.983
Now herbivores eat.

9
00:00:28.823 --> 00:00:33.723
They ingest 1,800 kilojoules, which is 30% % of the net primary production.

10
00:00:34.643 --> 00:00:37.303
The other 4,200 is never grazed.

11
00:00:37.843 --> 00:00:39.563
It dies and enters detritus.

12
00:00:40.403 --> 00:00:45.483
Detritus is dead matter that feeds bacteria, fungi and animals that eat detritus.

13
00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:47.697
Follow the herbivores.

14
00:00:48.617 --> 00:00:49.637
They ingest 1,800.

15
00:00:50.857 --> 00:00:52.737
They egest 1,080 as feces.

16
00:00:53.757 --> 00:00:56.277
The other 720 is assimilated.

17
00:00:57.037 --> 00:00:59.617
The herbivores respire 360 as heat.

18
00:01:00.397 --> 00:01:04.017
The last 360 is production, new tissue and offspring.

19
00:01:04.977 --> 00:01:07.757
The three efficiencies are 30, 40 and 50%.

20
00:01:07.757 --> 00:01:11.857
percent. Multiplied, they give a transfer efficiency of 6%.

21
00:01:11.857 --> 00:01:12.857
percent.

22
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.920
Predators keep the same books.

23
00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:19.420
Of the herbivores' 360 of production, they ingest 200.

24
00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.940
The other 160 goes to detritus.

25
00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:26.480
The predators egest 100 and respire 60.

26
00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:28.660
Their production is 40.

27
00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:33.780
That is a transfer efficiency of 11%, % against 6% for the first link.

28
00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:36.860
So no single number describes both links.

29
00:01:37.833 --> 00:01:43.813
Now the detritus. Ungrazed plants, feces and uneaten animal production all arrive

30
00:01:43.813 --> 00:01:47.113
there. Together they come to 5,540.

31
00:01:48.373 --> 00:01:52.133
The decomposers respire 3,240 of it as heat.

32
00:01:52.933 --> 00:01:54.153
That leaves 2,300.

33
00:01:55.353 --> 00:01:59.113
Notice that the decomposers respired more than every animal combined.

34
00:02:00.033 --> 00:02:03.793
In this budget, most net primary production never passed through an animal.

35
00:02:03.793 --> 00:02:04.673
The decomposers respired more than every animal.

36
00:02:04.817 --> 00:02:09.577
Now add it up. Respiration totals 9,660.

37
00:02:09.577 --> 00:02:15.997
12,000 fixed, minus that, leaves net ecosystem production of 2,340.

38
00:02:17.077 --> 00:02:19.777
That is the detritus plus the predators' production.

39
00:02:20.677 --> 00:02:21.677
The ledger closes.

40
00:02:22.717 --> 00:02:24.957
Suppose each step passes on 10%.

41
00:02:24.957 --> 00:02:29.557
Then level four gets a tenth of one percent of net primary production.

42
00:02:30.337 --> 00:02:34.337
But 10% % is a rough benchmark from aquatic models, not a law.

43
00:02:35.277 --> 00:02:38.517
Keep rates in matching units, and keep the detritus in the budget.
